<header><h1>Date picker</h1></header>

<section id="introduction">
  <p class="introduction">The <strong>Date picker</strong> is a two-month React date-range control. It supports keyboard-focusable dates, adjacent-month navigation, range preview on hover, clear, today, and an optional Apply step for filters.</p>
  <p class="introduction">It uses <a href="https://react.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">React</a> and <a href="https://date-fns.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">date-fns</a>. Pass controlled <code>startDate</code> and <code>endDate</code> values (or <code>null</code>) and receive changes through <code>onChange(startDate, endDate)</code>.</p>
</section>

<section id="inline-date-picker">
  <header><h2>Inline date picker</h2></header>
  <p>Set <code>inline</code> when the range picker should be visible as part of a form or dialog. A selection is reported as soon as the second date is chosen; select a new date after completing a range to start over.</p>
  <div class="section-example"><div id="date-picker-demo-inline"></div></div>
  <div class="code-example"><pre><code class="javascript">const [range, setRange] = useState({ start: null, end: null });

&lt;DatePicker
  inline
  startDate={range.start}
  endDate={range.end}
  onChange={(start, end) =&gt; setRange({ start, end })}
/&gt;;</code></pre></div>
</section>

<section id="dropdown-date-picker">
  <header><h2>Dropdown date picker</h2></header>
  <p>Without <code>inline</code>, the component becomes a compact trigger and dropdown panel, matching the Scout date filter pattern. Picks remain temporary until Apply; Clear resets the controlled range and closes the panel.</p>
  <div class="section-example"><div id="date-picker-demo-dropdown"></div></div>
  <div class="code-example"><pre><code class="javascript">&lt;DatePicker
  startDate={startDate}
  endDate={endDate}
  label="Filter by date"
  onChange={(start, end) =&gt; setFilters({ startDate: start, endDate: end })}
/&gt;;</code></pre></div>
</section>

<section id="date-picker-behaviour">
  <header><h2>Behaviour</h2></header>
  <p>The picker always displays two consecutive months. Previous and next controls move them together, while Today returns the left calendar to the current month. Use the From and To date fields in the footer when an exact date is quicker to type; entering the dates in reverse order automatically normalizes the selected range. Dates outside a displayed month are shown only to complete the calendar grid and cannot be selected.</p>
</section>

<section id="date-picker-props">
  <header><h2>Props</h2></header>
  <table class="striped">
    <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th><code>startDate</code></th><td><code>Date</code> or <code>null</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>The first day of the selected range.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>endDate</code></th><td><code>Date</code> or <code>null</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>The last day of the selected range.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>onChange</code></th><td><code>(startDate, endDate) =&gt; void</code></td><td></td><td>Called with the new range. Inline pickers call it on every pick; dropdown pickers only when Apply or Clear is pressed. Both values are <code>null</code> after Clear.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>inline</code></th><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Shows the calendars directly instead of behind a dropdown button.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>label</code></th><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>"Date range"</code></td><td>Text on the dropdown button while no date is selected.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<script type="module" src="/scripts/date-picker-demo.js"></script>
